fix(ci): install bun in publish-npm (release.yml) (#159)

* fix(ci): install bun in publish-npm so prepublishOnly's build:daemon:dist works

The v3.14.1 release run (and the v3.15.0 run we just cancelled) both failed
at publish-npm with:

  Error: bun --version failed
    at run (scripts/build-daemon-binary.mjs:26:11)

Root cause: `npm publish` invokes the `prepublishOnly` hook, which runs
`npm run build && npm run build:daemon:dist && npm run build:bin`. The
build:daemon:dist step shells out to bun via scripts/build-daemon-binary.mjs.
The publish-npm job runs on ubuntu-latest, which doesn't ship with bun.

The build-binaries job already does `oven-sh/setup-bun@v2` for exactly the
same compile step. Mirror that setup in publish-npm.

* fix(ci): also unblock workflow_dispatch path for publish-npm + update-homebrew

PR #159 fixed the bun-missing-in-publish-npm bug. This expands the fix to
make the full release pipeline reachable via workflow_dispatch, not just
the original release: published event.

Why this matters: when a release: published run fails partway through
(as v3.14.1 and v3.15.0 did at publish-npm), the only recovery paths were
(a) delete + recreate the GitHub Release to fire a new published event,
or (b) manually run npm publish + dispatch to the tap. (a) is ugly and
(b) bypasses CI guarantees.

With this patch, workflow_dispatch with the tag input becomes a clean
re-run for the publish-npm + update-homebrew jobs:

  gh workflow run release.yml --ref v3.15.0 -f tag=v3.15.0

workflow_dispatch is privileged (repo-write required) so this isn't a
broadening of who can publish — it's a recovery path for failed runs.

Changes:
  - publish-npm: drop release-only gate; checkout the tag ref on dispatch.
  - update-homebrew: drop release-only gate; resolve version from inputs.tag
    on dispatch (github.ref_name on workflow_dispatch is the dispatch branch,
    not the tag).

